# STIG CD16-00-012200: PostgreSQL must implement NIST FIPS 140-2 or 140-3 validated cryptographic modul
# STIG ID: V-261965 (MEDIUM)

META
    esp_id `pg16-cd16-00-012200-fips-crypto-module-001`
    version `1.0.0`
    dsl_schema_version `1.0.0`
    platform `pg16`
    criticality `high`

    title `STIG CD16-00-012200: PostgreSQL must implement NIST FIPS 140-2 or 140-3 validated cryptographic modul`
    description `PostgreSQL must implement NIST FIPS 140-2 or 140-3 validated cryptographic modules to generate and validate cryptographic hashes.`
    author `example-security`
    tags `pg16,stig,disa-stig`

    control_mapping `DISA-STIG:CD16-00-012200,NIST-800-53:SC-13`
    control_objective `SC-13`

    assessment_method `TEST`
    implementation_status `implemented`
    responsible_role `dba`

    control_origination `sp-system`
    inherited_from `PostgreSQL16:localhost:pg-hardening`
    customer_responsibility `configuration`

    remediation_days `30`
    recommendation `Review and update the configuration file to meet compliance requirements.`

    component_id `comp-pg16-db`

    impl_SC_13 `PostgreSQL implements this control by validating the content of critical configuration files against required security settings.`

META_END

DEF
    OBJECT target_file
        path `/proc/sys/crypto/fips_enabled`
    OBJECT_END

    STATE content_check
        content string contains `1`
    STATE_END

    CRI AND
        CTN file_content
            TEST all all AND
            STATE_REF content_check
            OBJECT_REF target_file
        CTN_END
    CRI_END
DEF_END
